{
  "title": "SetLocalLoiter",
  "messageId": "0426",
  "isCommand": true,
  "description": "This message is used to command the vehicle to loiter about a desired position in the local reference frame. Note that in some applications, particularly air and undersea, position may be a mix of local coordinates for XY position and absolute coordinates for Z/altitude/depth.  This only applies if the Z axis for the vehicle coordinate frame is aligned with a vertical axis, e.g. a vector orthogonal to the ground plane.  In all other cases, implementations must use Zlocal reporting only. For example, a UUV launched from a USV may need to navigate using local X/Y coordinates based on its launch point (using dead reckoning from its IMU) but rely on direct readings that do not suffer from drift for its Depth and/or Altitude ASF. All times are in Coordinated Universal Time (UTC).",
